  "gate_answer": "The gate adds NOTHING. By construction V6 equals the fast variant exactly on the rows where the trigger fires and the slow variant exactly where it does not; the numbers confirm this to machine precision. Because fast LOSES on the fired rows, gating strictly dilutes the slow variant's gain. V7's persistence window makes it worse still. Selective fast adaptation cannot help when fast adaptation is harmful in the very rows selected for it.",
